<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">European Commission</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1958">1958</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The European Commission is the executive body of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>, which proposes legislation, enforces the treaties and manages common policies. It grew from the High Authority of the European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">Coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a> Community and the commissions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">European Economic Community</a> and Euratom, which merged in 1967. Its president is one of the most powerful figures in European politics; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luxembourgers">Luxembourgers</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaston-thorn">Gaston Thorn</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-santer">Jacques Santer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-claude-juncker">Jean-Claude Juncker</a> each held the post.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/european-commission.jpg" alt="European Commission" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EmDee · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belgique_-_Bruxelles_-_Schuman_-_Berlaymont_-_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…process: Joseph Bech was among the founding statesmen, Robert Schuman was born in the city, the Werner Report of 1970, prepared under Pierre Werner, first set out a plan for economic and monetary union, and Gaston Thorn, Jacques Santer and Jean-Claude Juncker each presided over the <b>European Commission</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-luxembourg">Grand Duchy of Luxembourg · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>After 1945 Belgium became a builder of the new Europe: Paul-Henri Spaak was a leading architect of the Treaty of Rome, Belgium co-founded Benelux, NATO and the European Communities, and Brussels became the main seat of the <b>European Commission</b> and the Council and, from 1967, of NATO’s headquarters.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Kingdom of Belgium · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Since 2013 the independence of judges and prosecutors has been doubted at home and abroad, Turkey has more cases pending at the European Court of Human Rights than any other country, and the <b>European Commission</b>'s 2023 report criticised its institutions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>The principle reached beyond the nation state: the European Parliament can dismiss the <b>European Commission</b>, and in 1999 the whole Commission resigned rather than face such a vote.</blockquote><a href="/government/parliamentary-democracy">Parliamentary democracy · Impact &amp; Legacy</a></li></ul></section>
